{# Colors
   Use the color to tell what the button does: primary for the main action of the
   page, default (a neutral gray) for the rest and danger for actions that delete
   or can't be undone. When no variant is set, each color uses its own style: solid
   for primary, outline for default and light for the other colors. #}
<twig:ea:Button type="button">Cancel</twig:ea:Button>
<twig:ea:Button color="primary" type="button">Save changes</twig:ea:Button>
<twig:ea:Button color="success" type="button">Approve</twig:ea:Button>
<twig:ea:Button color="warning" type="button">Suspend account</twig:ea:Button>
<twig:ea:Button color="danger" type="button">Delete</twig:ea:Button>
<twig:ea:Button color="info" type="button">View report</twig:ea:Button>
